when france fell to germany in may 1940  britain was left standing alone  well sort of alone alone in the sense of  it was only britain and all of its  empire remaining in the fight  irrespective the united kingdom's  position at that point wasn't exactly  enviable and there were many politicians  there who thought the fighting on was  foolish  so given britain's outlook at this point  this raises the question  why didn't britain make peace after the  fall of france so as you know  1940 saw the german invasion of denmark  norway the benelux region and france and  to put him mildly things didn't go well  for the allies  after the fall of norway britain's prime  minister neville chamberlain was under a  lot of pressure to resign and there were  two candidates to succeed him  lord halifax who said no thus narrowing  it down to only one candidate winston  churchill during this time the british  government was divided as to whether or  not it should continue the war  so far things hadn't exactly gone well  and the odds only seemed to be getting  worse and worse  this was mostly because france was  faring poorly at this point  which through the british strategy of  letting the french get punched in the  face until britain could harm and train  up an army of about one and a half  million men and send them to the  continent  which was planned for about 1942 with  france about to fall lord halifax pushed  to make peace and negotiate fire  mussolini's government this wasn't  because halifax thought that britain was  going to be conquered or mostly put in  charge or something but because he  didn't think that any victory was worth  a world war one style war of attrition  as you'll know halifax's proposals went  nowhere but why was that the case  there were several reasons the first was  that churchill and many  in government didn't trust any treaty  that hitler was willing to sign  furthermore one of germany's conditions  for peace was the return of its former  african and asian colonies which was not  something that the allies were willing  to countenance  the second reason was that british  military leadership was confident that  they could at worst push germany to a  stalemate  and at best last until the german  economy collapsed just like in world war  one  so for them it was simply a case of  keeping public morale up and not  bankrupt in the country by keeping the  sea lanes open  this opinion was solidified when italy  joined the war and but it decided to  focus on italy the idea being that just  like austria-hungary in the last world  war germany would constantly have to  bail them out  the third reason was that britain was  confident that germany would eventually  do something silly like invade the  soviet union or do something that would  pull the united states into the war this  wasn't due to some hunch but because  britain and polish code breakers had  heard it from the germans themselves  and to help secure support from the us  britain was sure to fight the war on as  many fronts as possible  for example by quickly sending troops to  greece when it was invaded this wasn't  because they thought they could stop its  fool but because it made it clear that  they were the ones defending smaller  nations independence were on the side of  international stability  which would indirectly put pressure on  american politicians to eventually do  something  britain's leadership didn't believe that  it could conventionally defeat germany  but that it simply had to hold out until  about 1942 until germany made a mistake  which it did in 1941 and soon afterwards  its ally japan did the same  bringing two monumental allies into the  conflict and tipping the scales  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons  james bissonette kelly money maker  marvin cassal mo aaron the white  james castaneda marcus arsenal jordan  longley gustav swann rasheed ali  jerry lambda maggie patzkowski  copperton